(3333207, 461503, 69102, '<td valign="top">i understand that "personification" doesn''t mean the image or the thing photographed has to look human, however I think that the best shots from this challenge convey the idea of personification, and the emotions and feelings being personified clearly. if I have to read the title of the image to understand what the photographer intends, then that falls short of fulfilling the idea behind the challenge (though that does not necessarily mean that the photograph merits a dnmc). without your title, this is just a high contrast, close crop shot of a bird''s head. it''s an interesting shot, and I like the detail of the bird''s skin that you have captured, but I don''t think (personal opinion) that it deserves to rate high in this challenge, because (again for me) when I look at the picture I do not think - "oh, that''s an interesting use of personification." sorry, still a 4.</td>', 'i understand that "personification" doesn''t mean the image or the thing photographed has to look human, however I think that the best shots from this challenge convey the idea of personification, and the emotions and feelings being personified clearly. if I have to read the title of the image to understand what the photographer intends, then that falls short of fulfilling the idea behind the challenge (though that does not necessarily mean that the photograph merits a dnmc). without your title, this is just a high contrast, close crop shot of a bird''s head. it''s an interesting shot, and I like the detail of the bird''s skin that you have captured, but I don''t think (personal opinion) that it deserves to rate high in this challenge, because (again for me) when I look at the picture I do not think - "oh, that''s an interesting use of personification." sorry, still a 4.', '2007-02-05 23:50:41.000000', NULL, 1),
