(3362691, 461343, 37730, '<td valign="top">This may be black and white but it should definitely be done in ''blue''!  imho<br/> <br/>A photograph is neither taken nor seized by force.<br/>It offers itself up. It is the photo that takes you. ~ Henri Cartier-Bresson<br/> <br/>Your photograph is a wonderful example of what Cartier-Bresson spoke.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-02-18 19:44:06.</i></td>', 'This may be black and white but it should definitely be done in ''blue''!  imho A photograph is neither taken nor seized by force.It offers itself up. It is the photo that takes you. ~ Henri Cartier-Bresson Your photograph is a wonderful example of what Cartier-Bresson spoke.', '2007-02-13 21:50:19.000000', '2007-02-18 19:44:06.000000', 0),
(3362703, 463965, 74059, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by emayner:</b></div><hr/><i> Actually, I knew it was not a real fetus, but my objection was to the insinuation that a fetus is not a person.i.e. justification for abortion.  The fact is, I did not vote on this entry, I just made the comment. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Had he used a <i>real</i> fetus and called it a personification then your point would have been well taken.  He is saying that <i>this</i> image is a personification <i>of</i> a fetus.  <br/> <br/>Beautiful color by the way...very nice shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by emayner: Actually, I knew it was not a real fetus, but my objection was to the insinuation that a fetus is not a person.i.e. justification for abortion.  The fact is, I did not vote on this entry, I just made the comment.   Had he used a real fetus and called it a personification then your point would have been well taken.  He is saying that this image is a personification of a fetus.   Beautiful color by the way...very nice shot.', '2007-02-13 21:53:46.000000', NULL, 0),
